ill for about 10h. The aim of this step is to ensure that soft steps magnetic particles are coated sufficiently by surfactant:. The whole process can be shown in Figure 2","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":54.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":48.333333333333336,"r":293.3333333333333,"t":174.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,576],"page_no":1},{"bbox":{"b":255.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":307.3333333333333,"r":550.3333333333334,"t":281.33333333333337},"charspan":[577,678],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/24","text":"2.2. Preparation of MRF. The preparation of MRF can be realized by existing technology [18,19]. The detailed can be described as follows. Firstly, carrier liquid and surfactant are mixed with certain proportion in a container: The mixture is stirred evenly under water-bathing at 50'C in blender for 2 hours. Then; soft magnetic particles are poured slowly into the container while the blender is running: The particles are evenly  distributed in the step. Secondly, the mixture is milled in planetary ball mill for about 10h. The aim of this step is to ensure that soft steps magnetic particles are coated sufficiently by surfactant:. The whole process can be shown in Figure 2"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Keep the ingredients of MRF samples identical except for particle size. And the volume fractions of soft magnetic par ticles are 20%. The details of soft magnetic particles (carbonyl iron powder; purchased from Jiangsu Tianyi Ultrafine Metal Powder co. Ltd ) and the index of samples are given in Table 1.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":199.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":306.3333333333333,"r":551.0,"t":257.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,305],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/25","text":"Keep the ingredients of MRF samples identical except for particle size. And the volume fractions of soft magnetic par ticles are 20%. The details of soft magnetic particles (carbonyl iron powder; purchased from Jiangsu Tianyi Ultrafine Metal Powder co. Ltd ) and the index of samples are given in Table 1."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"3. Results and Discussion","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":172.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":307.6666666666667,"r":439.6666666666667,"t":185.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,25],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/26","text":"3. Results and Discussion"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"3.1. Shear Stress of MRF. The relation between shear stress and transmitted torque of MRF (T) can be expressed as follows [20, 21]:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":129.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":307.0,"r":550.3333333333334,"t":164.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,131],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/27","text":"3.1. Shear Stress of MRF. The relation between shear stress and transmitted torque of MRF (T) can be expressed as follows [20, 21]:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"2 T = 3 2h","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":98.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":354.0,"r":457.3333333333333,"t":121.0},"charspan":[0,10],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/28","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"radius of actuator disk, 7 is the viscosity of carrier liquid in zero magnetic fields; Aw is the rotative difference of speed","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":54.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":307.0,"r":550.6666666666666,"t":81.0},"charspan":[0,125],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/29","text":"radius of actuator disk, 7 is the viscosity of carrier liquid in zero magnetic fields; Aw is the rotative difference of speed"}],"version":"1.10.0"}